.Dd July 13, 2023
.Dt DUT 1
.Os
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm dut
.Nd disk usage calculator
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl cClsbphv
.Op Fl d Ar depth
.Op Fl i Ar indent
.Op Fl n Ar rows
.Op Fl t Ar threads
.Op Ar path...
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a multi-threaded disk usage calculator for Linux, capable of
de-duplicating hardlinks.
.
.Pp
If invoked without an argument,
.Nm
will calculate disk usage for the current working directory.  Otherwise,
.Nm
will do so for all directories listed in
.Ar path... .
.
.Ss Output Format
.Nm
shows a summary of all the files reachable from
.Ar path...
in a tree-like format.  Specifying multiple directories in
.Ar path...
will result in a dummy
.Dq Pq total
tree node being created at the bottom of the output.  The output has two
columns: a size column that displays the total size taken up by this
entry, and a
.Dq shared space
column that indicates the amount of this total taken up by files
hardlinked to other places in the filesystem.
.Pp
In the below example,
.Nm
displays the disk usage of
.Pa example
as 12 kilobytes, consisting of files
.Pa 1 , 2 ,
and
.Pa 3 . 1
and
.Pa 2
are indicated by the second column to be hardlinks, due to having a
non-zero shared size.  Because
.Pa example Ap s
second column is 0, we can assume that they are hardlinks of each
other, since they are the only hardlinks inside of
.Pa example .
If they were instead linked to files elsewhere on the filesystem,
.Pa example Ap s
shared size column would instead show that 8K is shared with other
directories.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ dut ./example
 4.0K  4.0K |- 2
 4.0K    0B |- 3
 4.0K  4.0K /- 1
  12K    0B example
.Ed
.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.
.It Fl c
Disable colorized output.  This has the same effect as a non-empty
value in the
.Ev NO_COLOR
environmental variable.
.
.It Fl C
Force colorized output.  This overrides the environmental variable
.Ev NO_COLOR .
.
.It Fl l
Don't deduplicate hardlinks when traversing the filesystem.  This option
causes
.Nm
to only show the first column of output.
.
.It Fl b
Show sizes in plain bytes intead of human readable format.
.
.It Fl s
Count size of files instead of size on disk.
.
.It Fl p
Display full path of files in the tree.
.It Fl x
Limit disk usage calculation to the set of filesystems that
.Ar path...
live on, or the filesystem of the current directory if none are given.
.
.It Fl d Ar depth
Limit the depth of the displayed tree to
.Ar depth
levels.
.
.It Fl i Ar indentation
Specify the number of spaces for each level of
.Ar indentation
in the displayed tree.  The default is 2.
.
.It Fl n Ar rows
Specify the number of
.Ar rows
to show.  The default is the terminal height minus 10.
.
.It Fl t Ar threads
Number of
.Ar threads
to use for scanning the filesystem.  The default is 4 or the number of
available CPUs, whichever is greater
.Po
see
.Xr sched_getaffinity 2
.Pc .
.
.It Fl h
Display a help message.
.
.It Fl v
Display version information.
.
.El
.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
If the
.Ev NO_COLOR
environmental variable has a non-empty value, then the output will not
include any color
.Po
see the
.Fl c
option and also
.Lk https://no-color.org/
.Pc .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr du 1 ,
.Xr ncdu 1 ,
.Xr dust 1 ,
.Xr gdu 1
